# Raw ICS fixtures are retained source-of-record payloads (see
# docs/sources/HOT_CLUBE.md and fixtures/hot-clube/metadata.json). Their
# exact byte content — including a genuine, documented mixed CRLF/LF
# quirk in the retained Hot Clube samples — must never be rewritten by
# git's line-ending conversion (core.autocrlf) on any platform.
*.ics -text

# Retained evidence for governed source investigations
# (docs/SOURCE_INVESTIGATION_POLICY.md) includes files whose evidence_class
# is DIRECT_EVIDENCE and byte_faithful: true — raw HTTP response bodies and
# headers acquired live from a real source. Their exact byte content must
# never be rewritten by git's line-ending conversion, on any platform, for
# the same reason as the ICS rule above — a byte-faithful claim that git
# silently mangled on checkout would no longer be true.
research/source-investigations/**/evidence/** -text
